{
  "item": "Skeleton03",
  "mu_name": "Elite Skeleton body",
  "mu_name_from": "Data/Skill/Skeleton03.bmd, the third of ZzzOpenData's three `AccessModel(MODEL_SKELETON1 + i, L\"Data\\\\Skill\\\\\", L\"Skeleton\", i + 1)`: the Elite Skeleton's body, drawn in place of the five body parts on a MODEL_PLAYER whose SubType is MODEL_SKELETON3.",
  "why_this_one": "The Dungeon's Elite Skeleton (EliteSkeleton.json). Skeleton01's bones with grey plate over them: 676 triangles in two meshes, the bone (486, bons) and the armour (190, bons_b).",
  "world": "lorencia",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "A worn part and not a monster model, and the rig says so before anything else does: 56 bones, one mesh, one action - a bind pose whose tracks hold the same value in every key. The 56 are the player's own by name, Bip01 through knife_gdf, hand_bofdgne01 and Bone01 to Bone08, plus one Box01 and four dummies that the player's rig lacks; the player has Mesh01 to Mesh04 and gfh that this lacks. Exactly the shape of an armour part beside player.bmd, and it goes on the same way - mu2.sh finds no motion in the rig and borrows the player's 283 clips through the shared actions library. See docs/rigging.md.\n\nThat is also what makes the monster it belongs to different from every other in the town. A skeleton on the fighting floor is Crowd.Figure on the player's rig, standing in the sword stance and swinging the sword attacks, which is what MU does: CreateMonster builds it with CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_PLAYER, ...) and sets SubType = MODEL_SKELETON1, and RenderCharacter's `else if (o->Type == MODEL_PLAYER && SubType in SKELETON1..3)` draws this one part with RenderPartObject in place of the five body parts.",
  "maps": 384,
  "sheets": {
    "bons": "bons.png",
    "bons_b": "bons_b.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Data/Skill/bons.OZJ (the bone sheet Skeleton01 and 02 share) and bons_b.OZJ, a 128-square of dark grey steel plate -- a studded pauldron, a cuirass with a boss, banded lames -- with pale highlights painted in, no alpha, from MuMain.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "bons": "bone",
    "bons_b": "painted_steel"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "bone as Skeleton01's. The armour is painted_steel, as Skeleton02's green plate: MU's metal as MU drew it, its highlights painted in.",
  "cutout_from": "Not declared: neither sheet has an alpha channel.",
  "maps_from": "Skeleton01's three times its 128-square sheets, as Skeleton02's.",
  "islands_from": "Twenty-two islands for 676 triangles. 0-12 are Skeleton01's thirteen bone islands to the triangle (486, on bons): bone. 13-21 (190, on bons_b) are the plate -- pauldrons, cuirass, lames -- in painted_steel. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default.",
